---
title: "Errors"
description: "Every exception Tarn raises, and what usually causes it."
---

## `ColumnNotFoundError` {#err-column-not-found}

A `col("x")` naming a column the frame does not have. Raised at `collect()`, not at
the point the expression was built, because the schema is only known once the plan is
resolved. The message lists the columns that *are* present.

## `AmbiguousExprError` {#err-ambiguous-expr}

Python's `and`, `or` or `not` applied to an expression. Use `&`, `|` and `~`, with
parentheses around the operands. See @sec-filter-predicate.

## `TypeMismatchError` {#err-type-mismatch}

A comparison or arithmetic operation between incompatible column types — most often a
string column that was expected to be a date, because the CSV inference did not
recognise the format. Fix it at the reader with `types=`.

## `DuplicateKeyError` {#err-duplicate-key}

A join whose right side has more than one row per key, when the join was declared
one-to-one with `validate="1:1"`. Without `validate=` the join silently multiplies
rows instead, which is why declaring the cardinality is worth the keystrokes.
